---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageShell from '../components/PageShell.astro';
---
<Layout title="AI & Control">
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <PageShell
    title="AI & Control"
    subtitle="A locally-running vision model watches the roots and drives the pump in a closed loop — HexaFlow waters plants only when they actually need it."
    badge="Automation"
  >
    <div style="display:grid;gap:2.5rem;">

      <!-- How it works -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display kinetic" data-kinetic="word" data-reveal style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1rem;">
          AI-Driven Operation
        </h2>
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1rem;">
          The locally-running AI model observes plant roots via camera and dispenses water
          incrementally — verifying adequate hydration before stopping the pump. The result is a
          closed-loop system that responds to actual plant conditions rather than a fixed timer.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1rem;">
          The vision model came out of extensive brainstorming on how to pump water through the system
          in a loop — until we realized a vision model could watch
          the roots and pump only the amount of water the plant actually needs.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1rem;">
          The vision model reads moisture straight from the camera feed and drives the pump accordingly,
          closing a <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">continuous feedback loop</strong> that prevents
          both overwatering and underwatering.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">
          The whole loop runs on a <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">Raspberry Pi Zero 2W</strong>, chosen for
          its balance of price, compatibility, and power: it runs full Linux and hosts our web UI, yet draws
          little enough to stay passively cooled. The main camera is an
          <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">InoMaker 1080p USB camera (130° FOV)</strong>, alongside two secondary
          cameras. The wide field of view covers most of the dome, and we went with USB because routing a Pi
          camera ribbon cable through the nanolab's tight channels wasn't going to happen. The vision model's
          job is to detect dry roots via the camera and trigger the pump only when needed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Vision model demo -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Vision Model in Action
        </h2>
        <div class="vm-demo">
          <video class="vm-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/ai-demo-poster.jpg"
                 aria-label="Vision model classifying roots as dry or wet in real time">
            <source src="/media/ai-demo.webm" type="video/webm" />
            <source src="/media/ai-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <div>
            <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1rem;">
              A live test of the root-moisture model. The camera watches the roots sitting in a hex-channel dome,
              and the bars show the model's confidence in real time.
            </p>
            <ol class="vm-steps">
              <li><strong>Dry roots</strong> — the model reads them as dry, up to 96% confident.</li>
              <li><strong>Roots moistened</strong> — once they're back in the dome, it flips to wet at 95%.</li>
              <li><strong>Roots dried out</strong> — after blotting them with a towel, it returns to dry at 100%.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="color:#64748b;font-size:0.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin:1rem 0 0;">
              That dry/wet call is what decides whether the pump runs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Dual modes -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Dual Configuration Modes
        </h2>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:1.25rem;">
          <div class="card reveal-1" style="border-color:rgba(212,160,23,0.3);">
            <div class="section-label">Drop Test Mode</div>
            <h3 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 0.75rem;">
              Drop Testing Configuration
            </h3>
            <ul style="color:#94a3b8;font-size:0.875rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem;">
              <li>AI disengages during the drop window</li>
              <li>Pumps continuously for the length of the drop</li>
              <li>Driven by a <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">150 mL/min (5000 RPM) pump</strong></li>
              <li>Fills toward the channels' <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">≈ 10.12 mL</strong> max capacity during the 2.2 s test window</li>
              <li>Maximizes channel fill during the microgravity event</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card reveal-2">
            <div class="section-label">Long-Term Mode</div>
            <h3 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 0.75rem;">
              Long-Term Growing Configuration
            </h3>
            <ul style="color:#94a3b8;font-size:0.875rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem;">
              <li>AI vision actively monitors root moisture</li>
              <li>Driven by a <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">1 mL/min pump</strong> for long-term operation</li>
              <li>Saves <strong style="color:#e2e8f0;">320mA</strong> versus the drop-test pump</li>
              <li>Fine-grained control over water delivery</li>
              <li>Adaptive data collection and imaging protocols</li>
              <li>TDS and pH sensors active</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Custom carrier board -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Custom PCB
        </h2>
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          A custom PCB consolidates every electronics connection into one board —
          simpler wiring, fewer failure points:
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:1rem;">
          {[
            { title:'Raspberry Pi Integration', desc:'Powered through the nanolab\'s USB Type-B port' },
            { title:'4-Camera USB Hub',          desc:'Embedded support for up to 4 cameras at once' },
            { title:'Direct ADC Embedding',       desc:'More reliable connections for analog sensors' },
            { title:'Consolidated Breakouts',     desc:'Power and signal breakouts in one place for simpler wiring' },
          ].map((f, i) => (
            <div class={`card reveal-${i + 1}`}>
              <h3 class="font-display" style="font-size:0.95rem;font-weight:700;color:#d4a017;margin:0 0 0.4rem;">{f.title}</h3>
              <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#64748b;margin:0;line-height:1.55;">{f.desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sensor selection rationale -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1rem;">
          Sensor Selection Rationale
        </h2>
        <p style="color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Every sensor was chosen for a concrete reason — and against a documented alternative:
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:1rem;">
          {[
            {
              pick:'BME680',
              role:'Temp / Humidity / VOC',
              over:'BME280 / CCS811',
              why:'Chosen for simplicity',
            },
            {
              pick:'Adafruit 4026',
              role:'Capacitive moisture probe',
              over:'Resistive probes',
              why:"Won't oxidize over time",
            },
            {
              pick:'Atlas Scientific pH Kit',
              role:'pH measurement',
              over:'Arduino Gravity pH',
              why:"Glass reed can't work in microgravity",
            },
            {
              pick:'TDS Sensor',
              role:'Dissolved nutrient load',
              over:'—',
              why:'Tracks nutrient concentration in the reservoir',
            },
            {
              pick:'NeoPixels',
              role:'Lighting',
              over:'—',
              why:'Programmable spectrum for the grow channel',
            },
          ].map((s, i) => (
            <div class={`card reveal-${i + 1}`}>
              <h3 class="font-display" style="font-size:0.95rem;font-weight:700;color:#d4a017;margin:0 0 0.35rem;">{s.pick}</h3>
              <p style="font-size:0.825rem;color:#fff;margin:0 0 0.4rem;line-height:1.5;">{s.role}</p>
              <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#64748b;margin:0 0 0.35rem;line-height:1.5;">
                Over <span style="color:#94a3b8;">{s.over}</span>
              </p>
              <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#64748b;margin:0;line-height:1.5;">{s.why}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Carrier board / hardware photos -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Hardware Photos
        </h2>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;">
          <div style="border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(212,160,23,0.15);" class="reveal-1">
            <figure class="depth-fig">
              <div class="df-glow" data-layer="far" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <img class="df-img" data-layer="mid" src="/images/ai-1.jpg" alt="HexaFlow PCB layout" loading="lazy"/>
              <div class="df-hex" data-layer="near" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            </figure>
            <div style="padding:0.5rem 0.85rem;background:#0d1e35;font-size:0.78rem;color:#64748b;">HexaFlow PCB layout</div>
          </div>
          <div style="border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(212,160,23,0.15);" class="reveal-2">
            <figure class="depth-fig">
              <div class="df-glow" data-layer="far" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <img class="df-img" data-layer="mid" src="/images/ai-2.jpg" alt="Raspberry Pi Zero 2W on the HexaFlow PCB" loading="lazy"/>
              <div class="df-hex" data-layer="near" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            </figure>
            <div style="padding:0.5rem 0.85rem;background:#0d1e35;font-size:0.78rem;color:#64748b;">Pi Zero 2W on the HexaFlow PCB</div>
          </div>
          <div style="border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(212,160,23,0.15);" class="reveal-3">
            <figure class="depth-fig">
              <div class="df-glow" data-layer="far" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <img class="df-img" data-layer="mid" src="/images/ai-3.jpg" alt="Assembled HexaFlow PCB" loading="lazy"/>
              <div class="df-hex" data-layer="near" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            </figure>
            <div style="padding:0.5rem 0.85rem;background:#0d1e35;font-size:0.78rem;color:#64748b;">Assembled HexaFlow PCB</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Control flowchart (Miro) -->
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Control Flowchart
        </h2>
        <div style="position:relative;aspect-ratio:6/5;border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(212,160,23,0.15);background:#fff;">
          <iframe src="https://miro.com/app/live-embed/uXjVGJtNO9k=/?focusWidget=3458764657227665425&embedMode=view_only_without_ui&embedId=477128908768"
                  title="HexaFlow control flowchart" loading="lazy"
                  style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0;"
                  scrolling="no" allow="fullscreen; clipboard-read; clipboard-write" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </PageShell>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .vm-demo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 300px) 1fr; gap: 1.75rem; align-items: center; }
  .vm-video { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1080 / 1850; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid rgba(212,160,23,0.2); background: #000; display: block; }
  .vm-steps { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .vm-steps li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .vm-steps strong { color: #e2e8f0; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .vm-demo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .vm-video { max-width: 300px; margin: 0 auto; } }
</style>
